rk for you but that brings us to the  twinkie defense which is a very derisive  term for a thing that actually happened  though it is incredibly misunderstood  the most common legal strategy for  defending murder suspects is to deny all  allegations and force the government to  prove every factual element of their  case but when there is no dispute that  the defendant committed the crime  defense counsel will often shift to the  defendant's mental state to show why the  defendant is not legally responsible for  the crime and at a minimum deserves a  less severe charge than first degree  murder and such was the case with dan  white a former san francisco city  supervisor who assassinated then-mayor  george moscone and supervisor harvey  milk in a rampage at city hall turned  himself into the police and then  confessed to the crime well i'm  definitely a law and order i campaigned  very hard on what i consider to be the  number one priority not only for my  district but for san francisco and that  is to make this a safe city now this has  been the subject of several movies but  here's the pertinent actual background  on january 8 1978 harvey milk became the  first openly gay elected official in the  history of california a fervent advocate  for gay rights milk's first official act  on the board was to introduce a bill  which passed almost unanimously  outlawing discrimination based on sexual  orientation in employment housing and  public accommodations milk's famously  brash brand of liberal politics  frequently brought him into conflict  with that of conservative fellow  supervisor dan white a 32 year old  former police officer and firefighter  for example white was the lone  dissenting vote against milk's  non-discrimination ordinance tensions  between the two began to reach a boiling  point when milk cast a deciding vote in  favor of opening a halfway home in  white's district for troubled  adolescents white stated that he felt  betrayed by milk who had initially  